                        "tags": [
                            "participle"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8ff59c2d-0aa3-42fe-a2a0-4093849fe33e",
                                "sense_id": "0f015cdc-e0dc-31c3-82e9-26be268f18ae",
                                "text": "― Поздно ― я обвенчана, я жена князя Верейского."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8602abc5-cf00-467c-99eb-984876cf8c3d",
                                "sense_id": "0f015cdc-e0dc-31c3-82e9-26be268f18ae",
                                "text": "Через полтора месяца он был обвенчан и поселился, как говорили, счастливым обладателем красавицы-жены и миллионов, в большом петербургском заново отделанном доме графов Безухих."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c0ecdaeb-96e0-4f7a-9a5f-9699bf923103",
                                "sense_id": "0f015cdc-e0dc-31c3-82e9-26be268f18ae",
                                "text": "― Стало быть, и я угадал, и вы угадали, ― спокойным тоном продолжал Ставрогин, ― вы правы: Марья Тимофеевна Лебядкина ― моя законная, обвенчанная со мною жена, в Петербурге, года четыре с половиной назад."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f21dbdcf-0fcb-47c7-a17d-7c2c908a6434",
                        "source_entry_id": "ecda8c6c-24a7-3601-91ed-8d7619b2eea4",
                        "source_sense_id": "0f015cdc-e0dc-31c3-82e9-26be268f18ae",
                        "target_lang_word": "wedded",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "wedded",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "117df062-b5c9-3abc-8e9e-45fac7a6805f",
                                        "entry_id": "4d910a8a-a531-3347-8cc3-f23727647484",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Joined in marriage."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "30711d6f-ef2b-364b-acba-071ed949447a",
                                        "entry_id": "4d910a8a-a531-3347-8cc3-f23727647484",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Joined as if in a marriage."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "05808817-e57b-4a2e-96de-971a19f86bad",
                                                "sense_id": "30711d6f-ef2b-364b-acba-071ed949447a",
                                                "text": "She was too wedded to the first thought that came into her mind to see that her second idea was better."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5a2efcd4-0545-425d-b3a7-c7c914f85b8e",
                                                "sense_id": "30711d6f-ef2b-364b-acba-071ed949447a",
                                                "text": "The future policy of the Bundesbahn in diesel traction is firmly wedded to high-speed engines with hydraulic transmissions, and has standardised on four—possibly five—types."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "82241398-bd2b-4f1f-ad96-6e46d4390976",
                                                "sense_id": "30711d6f-ef2b-364b-acba-071ed949447a",
                                                "text": "So instead what we have now is a marriage of inconvenience - and it's fair to say that since then, the two haven't exactly walked hand in hand into the sunset to enjoy a life of wedded bliss."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "wedded",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "05738fb7-5f38-3107-b945-117b1837d701",
                                        "entry_id": "5db1044f-bfd9-3f2b-8641-5511051ae5ef",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "simple past and past participle of wed"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "form-of",
                                            "participle",
                                            "past"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "de78cd27-8351-462a-98fa-d037039752a2",
                                                "sense_id": "05738fb7-5f38-3107-b945-117b1837d701",
                                                "text": "15th c., [1997], Thomas Malory, Eugène Vinaver ed.\nAnd kynge Lott of Lowthean and of Orkenay thenne wedded Margawse that was Gaweyns moder, and kynge Nentres of the land of Garlot wedded Elayne: al this was done at the request of kynge Uther."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7e56cc99-9fc8-4b03-9373-9d205335c731",
                                                "sense_id": "05738fb7-5f38-3107-b945-117b1837d701",
                                                "text": "Ross the Red, it is said, wedded a Danaan woman, Maga, daughter of Angus Ōg."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "27ca6971-083c-4e2a-a773-f447bd608a5d",
                                                "sense_id": "05738fb7-5f38-3107-b945-117b1837d701",
                                                "text": "Húrin wedded Morwen Eledhwen of the First House — and their children were Túrin and Nienor."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1779bfc7-4812-4428-8831-7071bf4131b8",
                                                "sense_id": "05738fb7-5f38-3107-b945-117b1837d701",
                                                "text": "But when he shall have wedded himself unto that duty so that he hath made it one with him as a bridegroom maketh himself one with his bride, then doth that duty become of a sudden very beautiful unto him and unto others."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b6b60739-0a26-4029-9718-7b6ab4941412",
                                                "sense_id": "05738fb7-5f38-3107-b945-117b1837d701",
                                                "text": "1986, St. John Chrysostom, On Marriage and Family Life, Catherine P. Roth & David Anderson tr. http://books.google.com/books?hl=en&id=hbMtKk-kiLMC&pg=PA112&lpg=PA112&sig=GVHA-ol3fLhiSzro9HX7X4Rs4hE\nShe was wedded wearing no golden robe but chastity, piety, generosity, and every other virtue."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "156a791b-5153-44ac-bde0-54d1f6a3b101",
                                                "sense_id": "05738fb7-5f38-3107-b945-117b1837d701",
                                                "text": "“Who would have thought she’d already been wedded and bedded?”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
